    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Special letters",
     "texto": [
      "German has three vowels with umlauts: **ä** (like the «e» in «bed»), **ö** (an «e» said with rounded lips) and **ü** (an «ee» said with rounded lips).",
      "The **ß** is the same as a double «s».",
      "The **h** at the start of a word is breathed, like English «h». After a vowel it is silent and only makes the vowel longer (sehr)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Survival phrases",
     "texto": [
      "**Bitte** = please; also «you're welcome». **Entschuldigung** = sorry, excuse me.",
      "**Ich verstehe nicht** = I don't understand. **Noch einmal, bitte** = again, please.",
      "**Wie schreibt man das?** = how do you spell it?"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
